~  PLDEVLST.DAT     18  July  1985
~
~  This file contains all the data for each device type required by PROMlink
~  - except for the device size which it gets from the programmer.  All the
~  different devices are catalogued by manufacturer and are stored in roughly 
~  numerically increasing order.  The actual format required is outlined below.
~
~  The first non-comment line (lines that begin with a ~ will be ignored)of
~  this file must be the number of manufacturers preceded by a vertical bar
~  (|) which allows PROMlink to dynamically size the arrays necessary to hold
~  the information in this file.  Changing any of the information in this file
~  does not require re-compilation of PROMlink.
~
~  All devices are grouped by manufacturer.  Each group of devices made by a
~  particular device manufacturer must be preceded by the manufacturer name.
~  The device manufacturer name (which must be less than 20 characters long) is
~  on a line by itself and preceded by a percent sign (%).  On the lines 
~  following the manufacturer name are the devices made by that manufacturer.
~  Each device name (which must have less than 11 characters) is followed by a
~  ":" which is followed by the family/pinout code for that device.  Each
~  family/pinout code must be followed by a comma OR if it is the last device 
~  for that manufacturer, it must be followed by a carriage return or period
~  (but NOT a comma!).  Any number of devices may be listed on a line and 
~  spaces, carriage returns and line feeds may follow the comma after the 
~  family/pinout code.  Spaces or carriage returns and line feeds may NOT be
~  inserted between the device name and its family/pinout code, however.
~  
|35
